    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d664">

                <pb facs="0719" n="607" sameAs="frus:frus1919Russia/pg607"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.00/3682: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Chargé in
                        Russia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Poole</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-01-24T14:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">January 24,
                                1919, 2 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Telegraph American Mission Paris and Department at once answers to
                        following:<anchor n="4" xml:id="d664-f1"/> “1st, what is present attitude of
                    the Russians towards Allied intervention? 2d, what is the attitude of the
                    Archangel Government toward Kolchak? 3d, what are plans of Archangel Government
                    for spring campaign? 4th, to what extent is present Government supported in and
                    outside Archangel?</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d664-f1" n="4" xml:id="d664-f1-content">
                <p>For answers see telegrams from the Chargé in Russia, no. 793, Jan. 27, 3 p.m.,
                        <ref target="#pg608">p. 608</ref>, no. 794, Jan. 27, 4 p.m., <ref
                        target="#pg610">p. 610</ref>, and no. 812, Jan, 30, 5 p.m., <ref
                        target="#pg37">p. 37</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
